messages.content:
## Direct Recommendation

Enhance codx-junior with **two complementary views** that integrate seamlessly alongside the existing Kanban board:

1. **Planning View** – A prioritized, time-aware task list with drag‑and‑drop ranking, due dates, and workload indicators. It helps teams decide *what to do next* and keeps priorities explicit.
2. **Follow‑up View** – A live dashboard that surfaces progress, bottlenecks, and overdue work. It gives project managers an at‑a‑glance overview of team activity and task health.

Both views reuse the existing `Chat`/`Kanban` data model (extended with a few planning‑oriented fields) and share the same sidebar navigation pattern as the Kanban board. They are accessed via a new **Workspace navigation bar** at the top of the Kanban area.

---

## Specifications Table

| Area                | Planning View                                                                 | Follow‑up View                                                                 |
|---------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Primary Purpose** | Prioritize & schedule tasks                                                    | Monitor progress, identify blockers and overdue items                         |
| **Main Layout**     | Two‑column: left = prioritized task list; right = optional task detail panel   | Grid of metric cards + a list of tasks needing attention                      |
| **Key Components**  | `TaskPriorityList`, `TaskCard`, `DueDateBadge`, `DragHandle`, `QuickActions`   | `MetricCard`, `ProgressBar`, `OverdueList`, `ActivityFeed`, `AssigneeFilter`  |
| **Interactions**    | Drag‑and‑drop reordering, inline editing of priority/due date, quick status change | Filtering by assignee/board/column, click metric to drill down, expandable rows |
| **Data Source**     | `$storex.kanban.allBoards` (flattened), enriched with priority & due date       | Aggregated from all boards, real‑time updates via websocket events             |
| **Color Usage**     | Priority badges (high=red, medium=amber, low=green), due date warnings (overdue=red, today=amber) | Metric cards use neutral backgrounds; progress bars semantic colors            |
| **Typography**      | Task name `text-sm font-medium`, metadata `text-xs`, column headers `text-sm font-semibold` | Metric value `text-2xl font-bold`, label `text-xs uppercase tracking-wide`     |
| **Responsive**      | List collapses to single column on mobile, detail panel becomes bottom sheet   | Metric cards stack vertically on mobile, metric grid 2‑column on tablet        |
| **Accessibility**   | Proper `aria-label` for drag handles, keyboard accessible reordering           | Color not sole indicator for overdue; additional text/icon always present      |

---

## Code Examples

### 1. Workspace Navigation (refactor of top‑level view)

Create a new parent component that hosts the three sub‑views. Modify `App.vue` or the router to use this component.

**File:** `src/components/workspace/WorkspaceView.vue`

```vue
<script setup>
import KanbanBoardView from '@/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue'
import PlanningView from '@/components/planning/PlanningView.vue'
import FollowupView from '@/components/followup/FollowupView.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="workspace-view flex flex-col h-full bg-base-100">
    <!-- Top navigation tabs -->
    <div class="shrink-0 flex items-center gap-1 px-4 py-2 border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200">
      <button
        v-for="tab in tabs"
        :key="tab.id"
        @click="activeTab = tab.id"
        class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm gap-2 rounded-lg text-sm transition-all duration-150"
        :class="activeTab === tab.id ? 'bg-primary/10 text-primary' : 'text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300'"
      >
        <i :class="tab.icon" class="text-xs"></i>
        {{ tab.label }}
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Dynamic view area -->
    <div class="flex-1 overflow-hidden">
      <Transition name="fade" mode="out-in">
        <component :is="activeComponent" :key="activeTab" :project="project" />
      </Transition>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    project: { type: Object, default: null }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      activeTab: 'kanban',
      tabs: [
        { id: 'kanban', label: 'Board', icon: 'fa-solid fa-columns' },
        { id: 'planning', label: 'Planning', icon: 'fa-solid fa-list-check' },
        { id: 'followup', label: 'Follow‑up', icon: 'fa-solid fa-chart-line' }
      ]
    }
  },
  computed: {
    activeComponent() {
      return {
        kanban: KanbanBoardView,
        planning: PlanningView,
        followup: FollowupView
      }[this.activeTab]
    }
  }
}
</script>

<style scoped>
.fade-enter-active, .fade-leave-active { transition: opacity 0.15s ease; }
.fade-enter-from, .fade-leave-to { opacity: 0; }
</style>
```

### 2. Planning View – Prioritized Task List

**File:** `src/components/planning/PlanningView.vue`

```vue
<script setup>
import TaskPriorityList from './TaskPriorityList.vue'
import TaskDetailPanel from './TaskDetailPanel.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="planning-view flex h-full">
    <!-- Priority list (left) -->
    <div class="flex-1 overflow-auto p-4 border-r border-base-300">
      <TaskPriorityList
        :tasks="prioritizedTasks"
        @select-task="selectedTaskId = $event"
        @update-priority="onUpdatePriority"
        @update-due-date="onUpdateDueDate"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Detail panel (right, optional) -->
    <Transition name="slide-left">
      <TaskDetailPanel
        v-if="selectedTask"
        :task="selectedTask"
        class="w-80 shrink-0 border-l border-base-300 bg-base-200"
        @close="selectedTaskId = null"
        @status-change="onStatusChange"
      />
    </Transition>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    project: { type: Object, default: null }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      selectedTaskId: null,
      // Temporary priority list; in real app would come from store
      priorityOrder: ['high', 'medium', 'low']
    }
  },
  computed: {
    allTasks() {
      // Flatten all chats from all boards, add board name
      return this.$storex.kanban.allBoards.flatMap(board =>
        board.chats.map(chat => ({
          ...chat,
          boardTitle: board.title,
          boardId: board.id
        }))
      )
    },
    prioritizedTasks() {
      // Sort by priority then due date
      return [...this.allTasks].sort((a, b) => {
        const pa = this.priorityOrder.indexOf(a.priority || 'low')
        const pb = this.priorityOrder.indexOf(b.priority || 'low')
        if (pa !== pb) return pa - pb
        if (a.due_date && b.due_date) return new Date(a.due_date) - new Date(b.due_date)
        if (a.due_date) return -1
        if (b.due_date) return 1
        return a.name.localeCompare(b.name)
      })
    },
    selectedTask() {
      return this.prioritizedTasks.find(t => t.id === this.selectedTaskId)
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onUpdatePriority({ taskId, priority }) {
      this.$storex.kanban.updateTaskPriority(taskId, priority)
    },
    onUpdateDueDate({ taskId, dueDate }) {
      this.$storex.kanban.updateTaskDueDate(taskId, dueDate)
    },
    onStatusChange({ taskId, newColumn }) {
      this.$storex.kanban.moveTask({ taskId, toColumn: newColumn })
    }
  }
}
</script>

<style scoped>
.slide-left-enter-active, .slide-left-leave-active { transition: transform 0.2s ease; }
.slide-left-enter-from, .slide-left-leave-to { transform: translateX(100%); }
</style>
```

### 3. TaskPriorityList Component (with Drag & Drop)

**File:** `src/components/planning/TaskPriorityList.vue`

```vue
<script setup>
import TaskCard from './TaskCard.vue'
import { DragDropContext, Droppable, Draggable } from 'vuedraggable' // hypothetical, use actual library
</script>

<template>
  <div class="task-priority-list">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-base-content/80 uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">
      Prioritized Tasks
    </h2>
    <draggable
      v-model="localTasks"
      item-key="id"
      handle=".drag-handle"
      ghost-class="opacity-50"
      @end="onDragEnd"
      class="space-y-2"
    >
      <template #item="{ element: task, index }">
        <TaskCard
          :task="task"
          :index="index"
          @select="$emit('select-task', task.id)"
          @update-priority="$emit('update-priority', $event)"
          @update-due-date="$emit('update-due-date', $event)"
        />
      </template>
    </draggable>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    tasks: { type: Array, default: () => [] }
  },
  emits: ['select-task', 'update-priority', 'update-due-date'],
  data() {
    return {
      localTasks: [...this.tasks]
    }
  },
  watch: {
    tasks: {
      handler(newTasks) {
        this.localTasks = [...newTasks]
      },
      deep: true
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onDragEnd() {
      // Emit reorder event with new order of ids
      const orderedIds = this.localTasks.map(t => t.id)
      this.$storex.kanban.reorderTasksGlobal(orderedIds)
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

