I explored the project and confirmed the key integration points:

- `src/store/index.js` already registers `kanban` (and friends) and exposes `$storex` to components via a global mixin (`this.$storex.<module>`).
- `src/router/index.ts` maps `/kanban` → `KanbanBoardView.vue`.
- The store pattern is `typed-vuex` (`getterTree` / `mutationTree` / `actionTree`, namespaced modules).
- DaisyUI 5 + Tailwind tokens (`bg-base-100/200/300`, `border-base-100`, `text-base-content`, semantic `badge-error/warning/success`, `progress`) are the established visual language.

Below are the complete files to add/edit. No backend changes required — the planning/follow-up data is **mocked** in a dedicated store module so the views render immediately.

---

## What's included

| File | Action | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `src/store/planning.js` | **new** | Mocked planning/follow-up data + getters + actions |
| `src/store/index.js` | **edit** | Register the new `planning` module |
| `src/components/kanban/board/PlanningView.vue` | **new** | Prioritized, drag-reorderable task list + detail panel |
| `src/components/kanban/board/FollowupView.vue` | **new** | Metrics dashboard, attention queue, board progress, activity feed |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | **edit** | Add Board / Planning / Follow-up switcher tabs |

