| `src/store/planning.js` | `loadTasks()` now loops all pages (`while has_next`), aggregates into `rawChatsById`, guards with `MAX_PAGES`; task filter also accepts `mode === 'task'` | Only page 1 (100 of ~1180) was loaded — the view appeared frozen |
| `src/api/model/ChatSearchRequest.js` | Added `hasDateRange()`; `isValid()` / `getValidationErrors()` treat "query **or** date range" as valid | Makes the date-range-only semantics explicit and consistent |
| `src/store/chats.js` | *(optional)* plain-object branch also allows date-range-only | Consistency; not required because planning passes an instance |
| `api/codx/junior/db.py` | none | `Chat` already exposes `priority`, `due_date`, `progress`, `assignees`, `sort_index` |
| `src/api/modules/chats.js` | none | Already POSTs serialized `ChatSearchRequest` to `/api/chats/search` |
| Views (`PlanningView`, `FollowupView`, `KanbanBoardView`, `PlanningRangeFilter`) | none | Default range = last 30 days, ranges are Today/7/30/Custom (no "All"), and they render from the store getters |

**Result:** the request was always sent correctly — the planner simply never followed the paginated envelope. After this change `allTasks`, `metrics`, `needsAttention`, `boardProgress` and `activityFeed` reflect the **entire** date-range dataset (all ~1180 results), so the Planning and Follow-up views refresh correctly when the range changes.

