## 3. Why the views don't need changes

`PlanningView.vue` / `FollowupView.vue` / `KanbanBoardView.vue` all read `$storex.planning.hasMore` — that name is now **only a getter**, so every existing reference keeps working and can never be the target of a write.

## 4. If the error survives

The message names the **target**, so if it persists I need the **stack trace line**. Two things to check:

1. Any other file doing `something.hasMore = …` where `something` is not an object — grep the whole repo (the search index does **not** cover the newly added `store/planning.js`, `store/kanban.js` and `components/kanban/board/*`).
2. A component receiving `hasMore` as a **prop** and assigning it (`this.hasMore = …`) — Vue 3 props are readonly, so assigning `$props.hasMore` logs a warning, but assigning `this.hasMore` when `hasMore` is a boolean-local/hoisted value will throw this exact message.

